 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Plants are multicellular eukaryotes with cellulose cell walls and chlorophyll; they make food by photosynthesis and store it as starch.\nMain groups:\n• Non-flowering plants: mosses (no true roots, damp places), ferns (roots, stems, leaves; spores under the leaves), conifers (cones, needle leaves, seeds not in fruits).\n• Flowering plants (angiosperms): reproduce by flowers and seeds enclosed in fruits. Two classes:\n  monocotyledons (one seed leaf; e.g. maize, rice, grasses, palms, bananas) and dicotyledons (two seed leaves; e.g. beans, groundnuts, mango, cocoa, hibiscus).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "learn": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "What makes a plant",
    "text": "Plants are multicellular organisms whose cells have nuclei, cellulose walls and chloroplasts. They make their own food by photosynthesis and store it as starch: think of cassava roots, yam tubers and maize grains.\nThey are fixed in one place and grow throughout their lives."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Plants without flowers",
    "text": "• Mosses: small, soft plants of damp walls and tree trunks; no true roots (only rhizoids), no flowers, reproduce by spores.\n• Ferns: true roots, stems and leaves (fronds); brown spore patches under the fronds; no flowers or seeds.\n• Conifers: trees with needle-like leaves; seeds are carried in cones, not inside fruits."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Flowering plants",
    "text": "Flowering plants reproduce with flowers, and their seeds are enclosed in fruits. They are divided by the number of seed leaves (cotyledons) in the seed:\n• monocotyledons, one: maize, rice, sorghum, grasses, oil palm, banana, onion;\n• dicotyledons, two: beans, groundnuts, mango, cocoa, coffee, hibiscus.\nNext lesson compares them in detail."
   }
  ],
  "key_words": [
   {
    "word": "cotyledon",
    "meaning": "a seed leaf"
   },
   {
    "word": "monocotyledon",
    "meaning": "flowering plant with one seed leaf"
   },
   {
    "word": "dicotyledon",
    "meaning": "flowering plant with two seed leaves"
   },
   {
    "word": "angiosperm",
    "meaning": "a flowering plant with seeds in fruits"
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   "Moss: damp walls",
   "Fern: spores under fronds",
   "Maize: monocot",
   "Mango: dicot"
  ],
  "mistake": {
   "wrong": "Ferns reproduce by seeds",
   "right": "Ferns reproduce by spores",
   "why": "Ferns have no flowers and no seeds; spores form under their fronds."
  }
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
